---
/**
 * The short licence note that closes every pattern page.
 *
 * Deliberately states the permission first. Most patterns lead with prohibitions;
 * the thing a maker actually wants to know is whether they can sell what they make,
 * and here the answer is yes. Full terms live on /licence/.
 */
---

<aside class="licence">
	<h2>Using this pattern</h2>

	<p>
		This pattern is free. <strong>Make it, gift it, and sell what you make</strong> — no
		permission needed and no licence to buy. A credit and a link back are appreciated, but
		they are a courtesy, not a condition.
	</p>

	<p class="quiet">
		Please don't sell, republish or redistribute the pattern itself, and don't use my
		photographs without asking. Sharing it? Link to this page rather than copying the text —
		that way people get any corrections. <a href="/licence/">Full terms</a>.
	</p>
</aside>

<style>
	.licence {
		max-width: 620px;
		margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 60px);
		padding-top: 26px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		font: italic 400 22px/1 var(--serif);
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	p {
		margin: 0 0 14px;
		font: 400 15px/1.7 var(--sans);
		color: var(--ink-2);
	}

	p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	strong {
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--ink);
	}

	.quiet {
		font-size: 13.5px;
		color: var(--muted);
	}

	a {
		display: inline-block;
		padding-block: 5px;
		color: var(--terracotta);
	}
</style>
